  ## 13. The tool to look through emails + the local LLM is not good at searching through emails, for example when I say what emails did I get on the 8th of july this year, it says I did not get any which I did, and when I ask it for the most recent email I got it says I dont have any, as no emails match "from:me subject:recent" — ✔ fixed
  - **Root cause:** the old search was FTS-only over quoted tokens. It had no
    recency ("most recent" → a bm25 hit from months ago), no date support, and
    fed the Gmail-style operators the 4B emits (from:/subject:/on:/`||`) to FTS
    as literal text → 0 results. The date miss was also a **timezone** bug:
    received_at is UTC, so 3 emails whose *local* date was Jul 8 were stored as
    Jul 9 and never matched a naive Jul-8 filter.
  - **Done:** `parse_mail_query` in `email_menu.py` turns the operator/date
    query into structured filters (dates resolved in the user's local tz →
    UTC bounds), everything orders newest-first, and an empty query returns the
    most recent mail. The search_email tool description now steers the model
    (empty query for latest; on:/after:/before:; from:/subject:). Live-verified:
    "most recent email" → real newest; "emails on the 8th of july" → the 3 real
    Jul-8 (local) messages.

